\f0\fs24 \cf0 Search for new or missing data centre projects in Sweden.\
\
Scope:\
- Sweden only\
- one candidate must be one physical site in one Swedish bidding zone\
- do not create one candidate for a national, regional, or multi-site investment spanning several bidding zones\
- include hyperscale, AI/HPC, colocation, cloud, enterprise, and large edge projects\
- exclude ordinary server rooms unless reported as a data centre project\
- exclude GPU purchases, customer deployments, cloud launches, and equipment orders inside existing data centres unless the source identifies a new site, phase, expansion, or capacity claim\
- include only projects with public evidence\
\
Search for:\
- company announcements\
- municipal planning material\
- environmental permits\
- grid connection information\
- construction starts\
- investment decisions\
- operational openings\
- cancellations or dormancy\
- new phases or capacity claims for projects already in the master files\
\
Write candidates to:\
data/audit/new_project_candidates.csv\
\
Before writing a candidate, compare it with data/master/projects_master.csv and data/master/capacity_master.csv. If it appears to be a customer deployment or hardware purchase inside an existing project, do not write a candidate. If it may be a new phase of an existing site, explain the overlap in notes.\
\
Use docs/status_rules.md when judging whether a candidate could later be scenario-relevant. Scenario tags are public relevance tags, not additive accounting instructions. If a new phase sits inside a dated full-site or cumulative capacity path, explain that relationship in notes.\
\
For every MW figure, classify reported_capacity_basis from the exact source wording that supports the number. Do not infer basis from the project name, data centre type, or surrounding narrative. Use these values:\
- it_load: the source explicitly says IT load, IT capacity, critical IT load, critical load, critical power, compute capacity, IT-effekt, or separates X MW IT from Y MW power\
- facility_total: the source describes total facility power, total power, power capacity, power supply, site power, or similar facility-level power without an IT-specific qualifier\
- grid_connection: the source describes contracted, requested, secured, or available electrical connection/power access for the site: grid connection capacity, anslutningseffekt, contracted power, power feed, access to MW, or a MW figure from a permit, grid, or connection-process document. A company release can support grid_connection if the wording is clearly about site power access rather than a general headline capacity\
- unspecified_headline: the source only says X MW data centre, X MW campus, X MW site, up to X MW, gigawatt-scale, or similar headline wording without a clear qualifier\
- backup_generation: the source describes only backup generation, diesel reserve, or permitted backup power\
- reactor: the source describes reactor, SMR, or other generation capacity rather than load\
- rack_density: the source gives MW per rack, rack row, or similar density rather than campus capacity\
\
Do not set interpreted_it_load_mw equal to reported_capacity_mw unless reported_capacity_basis is it_load. For facility_total, grid_connection, and unspecified_headline, leave interpreted_it_load_mw blank unless there is a specific reason to propose a manual override. The build script will derive IT load from reported_capacity_mw / PUE. For unspecified_headline, use this grid-side/facility-side interpretation as the conservative default for headline MW figures. For backup_generation, reactor, and rack_density, leave interpreted_it_load_mw blank and explain the limitation in notes.\
\
Keep capacity_type and reported_capacity_basis separate. capacity_type should describe the row shape, such as facility_capacity, initial_phase_capacity, incremental_expansion, cumulative_site_capacity, or full_campus_potential. reported_capacity_basis should describe what the MW number means.\
\
Required fields:\
candidate_id\
developer\
project_name\
municipality\
county\
bidding_zone\
project_status\
investment_decision\
reported_capacity_mw\
reported_capacity_basis\
capacity_type\
interpreted_it_load_mw\
start_year\
construction_start_year\
source_url\
source_title\
source_date\
access_date\
evidence_excerpt\
confidence\
notes\
\
Do not add candidates to master data.}
